From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: 8192xb: add LCK

Keep the thermal value at init and redo the LO calibration from the RF
track work once either path drifts by 8 or more, as Realtek's
rtk_wifi6_ap driver does for this chip. The calibration puts both paths
in RX mode, retriggers path A and waits for the LPF to go idle.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8192xb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8192xb.c
@@ -1043,6 +1043,7 @@ static void rtw8192xb_rfk_init(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
 	rtwdev->is_tssi_mode[RF_PATH_A] = false;
 	rtwdev->is_tssi_mode[RF_PATH_B] = false;
 	memset(rfk_mcc, 0, sizeof(*rfk_mcc));
+	rtw8192xb_lck_init(rtwdev);
 
 	rtw8192xb_rck(rtwdev);
 	rtw8192xb_dack(rtwdev, RTW89_CHANCTX_0);
@@ -1065,6 +1066,11 @@ static void rtw8192xb_rfk_channel(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 	rtw89_btc_ntfy_conn_rfk(rtwdev, false);
 }
 
+static void rtw8192xb_rfk_track(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev)
+{
+	rtw8192xb_lck_track(rtwdev);
+}
+
